 ✧ Thinking
   I've hit an important finding while probing the Tissue API. The cell_tissue RC has several internal bugs that block meaningful tests:

   1. Record-shape mismatch: TissueNucleusBase getters read record.mask.*, but the primary constructor stores the mask record directly (and NucleusBase.evolve reads record.local.*). This makes Tissue([1,2,3]).toList() throw NoSuchMethodError, and deputy() crashes.
   2. Initial elements dropped: _Tissue.fromNucleus(..., elements: ...) never forwards elements to the storage init, so collections are always empty.
   3. Typos: inhertiable instead of inheritable, and testRule getter reads record.mask.testRule instead of record.mask.inheritable.testRule.

   These are small, mechanical fixes confined to cell_tissue (about 25 lines), and they align cell_tissue's record convention with the cell package's NucleusBase. Without them, any test of Tissue would either fail or codify broken behavior.

