   ## What the tests cover

   - Tissue([1,2,3]) factory: iteration, cast, elementAt, first, last, forEach, map, validate, context, isTerminal/isInvalidated/isGoverned, modifiable, async, equality, hashCode, toString, and auto-linking of initial Cell elements.
   - Tissue.governed with custom TestTissue, receptor, and synapses.
   - Tissue.empty() variants including the TissueNever sentinel (apply, deputy, async, operator +, iterator, etc.).
   - Tissue.fromNucleus / Tissue.create.
   - Tissue.deputy and nested deputies sharing storage.
   - Tissue.unmodifiable live view, deep cell projection, unmodifiableElement: false paths.
   - UnmodifiableTissue standalone/view/fromNucleus factories, including the identical(bind, elements) linking branch.
   - A minimal _DirectTissue extends TissueBase helper to exercise TissueBase's own ==, hashCode, iterator, and toString (normally shadowed by UnmodifiableTissueBase/ListMixin).

   ## Library bugs fixed (with your approval)

   All confined to packages/cell_tissue:

   1. Record-shape mismatch — TissueNucleusBase getters read record.local.*, but several constructors stored bare masks or (mask: ...). Normalized all nucleus records to (local: ..., principal: ...) across tissue_nucleus, tissue_list, tissue_map, tissue_set, tissue_queue, tissue_value.
   2. Initial elements dropped — UnmodifiableTissueBase didn't forward elements to TissueBase, so every Tissue was created empty.
   3. Typos — inhertiable → inheritable; testRule getter now reads local.inheritable.testRule.
   4. Deputies copied instead of sharing storage — _TissueDeputy now builds its override without an own container, so deputies share the principal's container (zero-copy).
   5. Unmodifiable view wasn't live — _UnmodifiableTissue.view no longer allocates its own container.
   6. **TissueContainer lacked content equality** — added ==/hashCode over the store (element-wise), so tissue == [1,2,3] works.
   7. Recursive dead defaults — Tissue.deputy and TissueBase.deputy had infinite-recursion default bodies; made them abstract (all concrete types already implement them).
   8. **TissueListNucleus.create used Set<E> instead of List<E>** for the deputy-local storage type.

   Notes:
   - dart analyze lib reports no errors (only pre-existing warnings/infos).
   - The pre-existing test/browser/tissue_test.dart still has its own compile errors (it's not part of this task); I left it untouched.
   - I removed my temporary tool/ probe scripts and the generated coverage/ directory.

