   ## Notable library bugs fixed during this batch

   TissueList
   1. TissueListMixin.apply was a stub (// ... implementation ...) — all mutations were no-ops. Implemented a full whitelist dispatcher plus 18 private mutation helpers (_add, _addAll, _insert, _sort, etc.).
   2. modifiable was missing setValueAt, setFirst, setAll, setRange, sort, shuffle.
   3. insertAll dispatched to insert; replaceRange dispatched to removeRange.
   4. removeAt/removeLast crashed on null apply results; made them null-safe with UnsupportedError.
   5. Unmodifiable base leaked the mutable modifiable set; added an empty override.
   6. ModifiableListAsync only had setValueAt; implemented all remaining async mutation methods; fixed unmodifiable async facade's Never inference.
   7. _UnmodifiableTissueList.deputy had an invalid this as TissueListBase cast; now resolves _nucleus.bind.

   TissueQueue
   1. TissueQueueBase declared an empty modifiable that overrode the mixin's real whitelist, so all mutable queue ops were no-ops.
   2. _removeFirst checked modifiable.contains(removeLast) and used container.last; fixed to removeFirst and container.first.
   3. addFirst/addLast/removeFirst were missing from modifiable.
   4. _remove used firstWhere (throws Bad state on miss); replaced with a null-safe lookup loop.
   5. _clear/_removeWhere/_retainWhere iterated lazily while removing (concurrent modification); materialized snapshots first.
   6. _addAll duplicated elements (batch pulse was mirrored back into the store); receptor now only fires for single-event batches.
   7. ModifiableQueueAsync.addFirst/addLast/removeFirst were hardcoded to throw; implemented them.
   8. Queue deputy used a root-nucleus override that broke storage sharing; switched to the same evolve(local: ...) pattern as the list deputy.
   9. _TissueQueueNucleus.evolve forced container: Container.queue in its local record, breaking deputy sharing; removed it (inherits from principal).
   10. Unmodifiable deputy cast and unmodifiable modifiable/async generic fixed.

   TissueValue
   1. _TissueValueDeputy passed a raw record into evolve(override: ...); fixed to use evolve(bind/testRule/synapses/principal:).
   2. == never considered other mutable TissueValues; added other.value == value.
   3. Unmodifiable bind-equality returned identical(unmodifiable, this) (always false); now compares other.value == value.
   4. Unmodifiable base leaked the set function in modifiable; added an empty override.

   ## Where TissueValue stands below target

   The remaining uncovered lines are concentrated in: _TissueValue.empty redirect lines, TissueValueBase constructor seed lines, a few comparison-operator branches, hashCode/toString in the mixin, and the lock != null branch of _UnmodifiableModifiableValueAsync.value. Several are only reachable with finalValue containers, which are currently broken in tissue_container.dart (_finalValueCreate returns V instead of ValueContainer<V>), so I avoided exercising that path
    rather than rewriting the container strategy mid-session.

