   ## What the tests cover

   - TissuePulse.batch, CollectiveTissuePulse.from, CollectiveTissuePulse.governed, empty batches.
   - + operator: event+event, event+collective, collective+collective (with flattening).
   - withStep/evolve chains, root/trace propagation.
   - TissueEventShell: iterator, +/evolve/withStep throwing UnsupportedError, scrutinize unlocking.
   - unmodifiable projections: factory, live delegation, withStep/evolve deriving new events, +, shell, root.
   - Real events: ElementAdded from TissueList.add, ElementRemoved from remove, ElementUpdated record payload (before/after/value) from TissueValue.set.
   - groupBy utility.

   ## Library bugs fixed

   1. CollectiveTissueEventBase.+ performed an invalid cast (this as TissuePulse<E>), crashing whenever you added anything to an existing collective. Rewrote it to flatten payload and build a _CollectiveTissueEvent<dynamic> without the bogus casts.

   ## Why pulse coverage is below 95%

   The remaining uncovered lines are almost all private/plumbing members that are unreachable from the public API:

