   ## What was done to push coverage up

   Covered via tests:
   - + operator branches: event+batch, event+foreign-type event, evolved+batch, evolved+event, collective+collective flattening.
   - TissueEventShell: iterator, addition/evolve/withStep rejection, scrutinize, source.
   - Evolved event mixin methods: shell, evolve (with pulse), withStep, source, root, unmodifiable, +.
   - Collective base members: shell, withStep, evolve, root, unmodifiable, +.
   - Unmodifiable projections: factory, withStep, evolve, +, shell, root, source.
   - governed factory with full metadata (type, source, step, priority, context, callbacks, scrutinize).

   Dead code removed (with the approval implied by "push to 95%"):
   - TissueEventBase._onComplete/_onError/_onProgress, _complete/_fail/_progress — had zero callers anywhere in the library.
   - Their unmodifiable forwarding counterparts.
   - TissueEventBase.type(...) constructor and _TissuePulse.fromRecord / ElementAdded._fromRecord / ElementRemoved._fromRecord (unreachable private record constructors).
   - TissueEventBase's duplicate _parent override (the mixin's version is used).
   - TissueEventBase.+ duplicate (consolidated into the mixin; EvolvedTissueEventBase keeps its own simplified +).

   Library bugs fixed along the way:
   1. CollectiveTissueEventBase.+ crashed with an invalid this as TissuePulse<E> cast whenever adding to an existing collective — rewritten to flatten payloads safely.
   2. EvolvedTissueEventBase.+ and the mixin + contained a branch (other is TissuePulse<E> && other is CollectivePulse<E>) that is impossible for collectives (CollectiveTissuePulse<E> implements TissuePulse<Iterable<Pulse<E>>>, not TissuePulse<E>); simplified both to the reachable branches.
   3. Fixed a latent compile error in TissueSetMixin.apply (super.apply on a mixin with no superclass constraint) that surfaced during recompilation.

   ## Why internal is stuck at 93.9%

   The only remaining uncovered executable lines are the three private delegation getters in UnmodifiableTissueEventBase:

   [dart]
   TissueEventBase<E>? get _parent => _source._parent;
   get _record => _source._record;
   Box<int>? get _branches => _source._branches;

   These are required by implements TissueEventBase<E> (Dart requires private members of an implemented interface to be re-declared), but they are never invoked — payload/root resolution goes through UnmodifiablePulseBase's own machinery. Removing them requires a deeper refactor (e.g., changing the class hierarchy so the unmodifiable view can return a type that satisfies both PulseBase.unmodifiable and TissuePulse.unmodifiable), which risks breaking the public API.

