 > what file type I should use to save this console output which can retain the formatting like color and style of the output text?

 ✦ To keep the colors and styling (which are produced by ANSI escape sequences), save it as a plain text file with the ANSI codes intact — conventionally using the extension:

   - **.ansi** (most common, e.g. output.ansi)
   - or **.ans, .log, or plain .txt** (all fine — the extension doesn't change the content)

   ## How to save it

   In your Git Bash / terminal:

   [bash]
   dart test 2>&1 | tee test-output.ansi

   or just redirect:

   [bash]
   dart test > test-output.ansi 2>&1

   tee shows the output live and saves it; > only saves.

   ## Important caveat

   The file itself contains raw escape sequences like \x1b[32m. They will only render as colors if you view the file with an ANSI-aware tool, for example:

   - cat test-output.ansi in a terminal
   - less -R test-output.ansi
   - VS Code with an ANSI color extension
   - Windows Terminal / ConEmu viewing the raw file

   If you open it in Notepad or a plain editor without ANSI support, you'll see the escape codes as garbage (←[32m etc.).

